  "body": "**Stacked on #2342** (`issue/796-tormach-wrapped-a`, Fixes #796). This branch starts from that PR's head `ef864e37d`; until #2342 merges, this PR's diff also shows its files. It merges after #2342. Fork synced at upstream main 4e8616b (through #2342's branch).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe continuous half of #1904: a step-by-step guide page for the Tormach 770MX + microARC 4, with a committed demo project and drawn pictures.\n\n- **Page:** `site/content/guide/getting-started/first-continuous-4axis-part.md`, \"Your first continuous 4-axis program\". It covers: how the bar is held; the machine file's four A values (axis, travel, `nose_to_axis`, A rate) and what to compare with the machine; finding the A centreline and setting G54 on it; the ball tool; a Rotary Parallel operation, setting by setting; the checks and what the stock simulation says; the posted program read line by line; what the post refuses; a run in the PathPilot simulator; then a single-block start and an air cut with no bar.\n- **What the post writes, in plain words, from the Hub readings on #796:** `G93` on a feed that turns A with X Y Z, and why (reading 2: in `G94` F is the X Y Z distance only; reading 3: `G93` is accepted and timed); the A rate cap worked out on real lines; an A-only feed in `G94` with F in degrees per minute (reading 4); A counting on through 180 (reading 1); `G94` back before the last rapid.\n- **Demo project:** `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj`, the program it posts `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.nc` (3213 lines) and the model `examples/models/first-continuous-4axis-part.obj` (made by `gen_first_continuous_4axis_part_obj.py`). #2342's kit project was not reused: it has no continuous operation, and its wrap golden has a stock that ends where the model ends.\n- **Pictures:** three SVG files in `site/static/guide-pictures/`, drawn from the committed project, model and program by `site/tools/first_continuous_4axis_pictures.py`: the bar and the work offset, each move unrolled (X against A), and the A word line by line with the G93 lines marked. No PNG, no screenshot. The UI renderer of #1902 (PR #2078) is not merged, so there are no UI renders yet.\n- **Links and corrections:** linked from Getting started, First run, \"Your first 4-axis part\", the Multi-axis index and \"Continuous 4-axis\". `continuous-4-axis.md` no longer says that no shipped post writes inverse-time feed, and the Multi-axis index no longer says that `tormach.cps` indexes A only (both untrue since #2342). `continuous-4-axis.md` has a new section \"End faces and the chuck\".\n- `docs/decisions/1904-continuous-4axis-walkthrough.md`.\n\n## Two findings that shape the page\n\n1. **The page ends with an air cut and tells the reader not to cut.** Rotary Parallel finishes both end faces of the model down to the axis. On a bar held in a chuck, the chuck-side end face is inside the bar: the program feeds to Z-0.03 at X-1.3125 while the stock goes on to X-2. With a 1/2 in flute the shank check blocks the post (good); with a longer flute it posts with no warning. No setting keeps the pass off an end face. Filed as **#2343**. The page says this at the top, in \"Check it\" and at the end.\n2. **Rotary Offset cannot be used on this machine file.** Each level that cuts takes two laps of A, and the post refuses the count past -360..360. Filed as **#2344**.\n\nThis is a partial delivery for #1904. The wrapped engraving or slot is unavailable. Neither program has a recorded PathPilot Hub run to M30. The guide describes an air cut, but no Hub run or machine run was done. Keep #1904 open for this acceptance work.\n\n## Review fixes\n\nInherited parent #2342 head `b93fe06131248f91e41e90104e0d050409add852` with a merge commit. Its feed-time calculation bounds the curved part-relative trajectory from the rounded posted words. The parent includes an independent trajectory pin. This child refreshes its example program for that safety correction. The guide now explains the curved trajectory bound. Its four excerpts, stated line numbers, feed calculations and generated SVG pictures remain valid without numeric changes.\n\nBoth NC comparisons allow tightly bounded platform rounding differences. The comparisons preserve line structure and exact nonnumeric words. The independent rate checks remain. The committed program refresh is required by the inherited safety fix, rather than used to hide platform differences.\n\nThis partial delivery uses `Refs #1904`. The issue stays open for the missing Hub runs to M30 and the wrapped engraving or slot.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/796-tormach-wrapped-a`: green (app suite `continuous_4axis_part`, 5 tests):\n  - `the_continuous_4axis_part_posts_its_wrapped_program`: the committed project is byte for byte the built document; G93 on each feed that turns A with X Y Z and on no other move; A never jumps; A inside the travel\n  - `the_committed_project_posts_the_committed_program`: loads with no notes, passes the machine check and the post gate\n  - `each_g93_move_holds_the_a_rate`\n  - `the_pass_cuts_the_chuck_side_end_face_to_the_centreline` (the fact behind \"air cut only\")\n  - `a_short_flute_is_blocked_at_the_chuck_side_end_face`\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test continuous_4axis_part -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests`: the 13 new tests of `test_first_continuous_4axis_part.py` pass (UI labels in their sources, tables against the project, G-code excerpts as runs of the program, stated line numbers and A range, quoted refusals in the post, pictures equal to the script's output, links). 46 of 49 pass. The 3 failures are the same on the unchanged base (`test_first_4axis_part ... test_machine_and_post_are_the_shipped_ones`, `test_guide_icons` x2) and are filed as #2345.\n- `zola check` in `site/`: 45 pages, no broken link.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run in the PathPilot Hub and none on a machine. The issue's \"Done means\" asks for a Hub run to M30: the page lists the five things to check and asks for the result on #1904.\n- The A direction on a real table, and PathPilot's own A limits (open in #2342).\n- The UI steps were written from the UI sources (each bold label is held to its source by the site test); the app was not driven by hand.\n- No feeds or speeds are recommended: the page says that its numbers are the example's.\n\nChangelog: none (docs and a test-held example)\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1904\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
